# Methods, Procs, Lambdas, Closures

## Methods

- named parametrized chunks of code:

def name(param, default_param=1, *remaining_params)
  ...
end 

- alias - define alternative name for an existing method: alias aka also_known_as

## Procs

- named representation of a block used in the iterator method:

def iter(a, &b)  # &b represents the input block, must be the last param
  ...
  b.call(...) # calling proc istead of using yield

- can be also created outside of iterator: a = Proc.new({block}) or a = lambda({block}) (then its called Lambda), or alternatively a = -> (x){x+1}
- invoking: a.call(2)
- proc behaves more like a block, lambda more like a method, both are closures
- closure retains bindings to variables used by the block
